## opensift continous deployment
CI/CD enables fast delivery cycles, high reliability, short feedback loops, and low lead times

# pipeline
- set of tasks with steps in order (build, test, release, deploy)
- each individual step requires a pod to be created - and a command is run in that pod
- relatively new addition to os
- under development, ongoing change from tekton engine to something else...

# resources required for pipeline:

task resource 
- steps -- items of tasks resource
- task has a pod 
- steps in a task create individual containers in the task pod (because they can use different images)
- 2 task scopes: *task* and *cluster task* (project vs cluster scoped)

pipeline resource
- consists of tasks

task run resource
pipeline run resource
- both used to test tasks/pipelines
- takes a resource as a template

parameter resource
- allow for parametrization of tasks and pipelines

workspace resource
- allows for communication between tasks and pipelines

trigger resource
- can run tasks and pipelines based on external events
- not well supported in cli and ui 
- new thing

# pipeline builder 
- ui tool to create pipelines
- you can define parameters -- script, version, workspace ...

# task specificaiton
- task kind: ClusterTask 
- result specification 
- working dir, volume mounts
- tekton cli to work with tasks
tkn <type> <command>
- describe tasks and pipelines
tkn t describe fetch-url
tkn p describe my-pipeline

tkn t start fetch-url
tkn p start my-pipeline

- check pipeline runs:
tkn pr list
tkn pr logs my-pipeline-1

